    'Go has a vastly larger branching factor than chess, so the state space explodes and brute-force search is infeasible.');

  L('m1-3', 'm1', 'Potential and limitations of deep learning',
`**Deep learning** uses neural networks with many layers that learn hierarchical representations directly from raw data (pixels, text, audio).

**Potential**
• Excellent at perception tasks: image recognition, speech, translation, text generation.
• Learns features automatically, so less manual feature engineering.
• Scales with more data and compute.

**Limitations**
• Needs **large labelled data sets** and heavy compute.
• **Opaque** ("black box"): hard to explain individual decisions.
• Can be **brittle**: adversarial examples, poor generalisation to new conditions (distribution shift).
• Learns correlations, not causation; may pick up spurious patterns and biases in the data.
• Prone to **overconfidence** and, in generative models, hallucinations.`,
['Learns layered features from raw data', 'Strong at perception and language', 'Data and compute hungry', 'Black box, brittle under distribution shift', 'Correlation is not causation']);
