  L('m1-4', 'm1', 'Key breakthroughs in AI and ML',
`A short timeline worth knowing:

• **1950s**: Turing test (1950), Dartmouth workshop coins "artificial intelligence" (1956), the perceptron (1958).
• **1970s–80s**: expert systems boom; AI winters when promises are not met.
• **1986**: backpropagation popularised for training multi-layer networks.
• **1997**: Deep Blue beats Kasparov at chess (search, not learning).
• **2012**: AlexNet wins ImageNet using GPUs: start of the deep learning era.
• **2016**: AlphaGo beats Lee Sedol (deep RL plus tree search).
• **2017**: the **transformer** architecture ("Attention is all you need").
• **2022 onwards**: ChatGPT brings large language models to the mass market.

**Enablers** behind the recent surge: big data, cheap compute (GPUs/cloud), better algorithms (ReLU, dropout, attention) and open-source tools.`,
