  L('m1-5', 'm1', 'Supervised, unsupervised, semi-supervised and reinforcement learning',
`• **Supervised learning**: learns a mapping from inputs to a known label. Regression (continuous target, e.g. loss given default) or classification (default yes/no, fraud yes/no).
• **Unsupervised learning**: no labels; finds structure such as clusters or lower-dimensional representations (customer segmentation, anomaly detection, PCA).
• **Semi-supervised learning**: a small labelled set plus a large unlabelled set (fraud labels are scarce, transactions are plentiful).
• **Reinforcement learning**: an agent learns by trial and error which actions maximise cumulative reward (optimal trade execution, dynamic pricing, game playing).

Exam trick: look at **what data exists** (labels? feedback signal?) and **what the output is** (prediction, groups, or a policy of actions).`,
['Supervised: labels → prediction', 'Unsupervised: no labels → structure', 'Semi-supervised: few labels + many unlabelled', 'Reinforcement: actions + rewards → policy']);
  Q('m1-5', 'A trading desk wants an algorithm that learns how to split a large order over time to minimise market impact, using feedback on execution costs. Which approach fits best?',
