  L('m1-6', 'm1', 'Risks of inscrutability in AI and ML',
`**Inscrutability** (opacity) means humans cannot understand how a model reaches its outputs. Causes: model complexity (millions of parameters), proprietary vendor models, and high-dimensional data.

Risks:
• **Hard to validate**: errors, spurious correlations and bias can stay hidden.
• **Accountability gaps**: who is responsible when nobody can explain a decision?
• **Regulatory and legal risk**: customers may have a right to an explanation (e.g. adverse credit decisions, GDPR automated decisions).
• **Loss of trust** by users, customers and supervisors.
• **Difficult to detect drift or manipulation** in production.

Mitigants: prefer interpretable models where stakes are high, explainability tools (SHAP, LIME), documentation, human review and strong validation.`,
['Opacity hides errors and bias', 'Accountability and right-to-explanation issues', 'Mitigate with interpretable models, XAI, documentation, human review']);
  Q('m1-6', 'A lender uses a complex neural network to reject loan applications and cannot tell applicants why they were rejected. The MOST direct risk is:',
