  Q('m1-6', 'Why does inscrutability make model validation harder?',
    ['Validators cannot run the model', 'Spurious relationships and biases inside the model are harder to detect', 'Opaque models always have lower accuracy', 'Validation only applies to linear models'], 1,
    'If you cannot see how inputs drive outputs, you cannot easily check conceptual soundness or spot spurious drivers and bias.');

  L('m1-7', 'm1', 'Risks of over-reliance on AI systems',
`**Over-reliance** occurs when people trust AI outputs more than is warranted.

• **Automation bias**: humans accept system recommendations even when contradictory evidence exists.
• **Deskilling**: staff lose the expertise needed to spot errors or take over when the system fails.
• **Complacency** in monitoring: "the model has always been right".
• **Concentration and single points of failure**: many firms relying on the same model or vendor can create herding and systemic risk.
• **Out-of-distribution failures**: models trained on calm periods may fail in a crisis.

Controls: meaningful human-in-the-loop review, challenger models, fallbacks and manual procedures, training, and clear limits on where the model may be used.`,
