• **Unsupervised**: only X. Goal: find groups, structure or compressed representations.
• **Semi-supervised**: a few (X, y) pairs and many X without y. Goal: use the unlabelled data to improve the predictor.
• **Reinforcement**: no fixed data set; an agent interacts with an environment, receives rewards and learns a **policy**.

Typical finance examples: credit scoring (supervised), customer segmentation (unsupervised), fraud with scarce labels (semi-supervised), order execution or hedging strategies (reinforcement).`,
