  L('m2c1-5', 'm2c1', 'Data cleaning and why it matters',
`"Garbage in, garbage out": model quality is bounded by data quality.

Common cleaning tasks:
• **Missing values**: delete rows/columns, impute (mean/median/mode, model-based), or add a "missing" indicator. Ask *why* data is missing; non-random missingness can bias results.
• **Outliers**: detect (z-scores, IQR, visual checks) and decide: correct errors, cap (winsorise), transform or keep genuine extremes (tail events matter in risk!).
• **Duplicates and inconsistencies**: units, formats, spelling, dates.
• **Errors**: impossible values (negative age), wrong labels.

Reasons: better accuracy, less bias, valid inference, regulatory data-quality expectations (e.g. BCBS 239) and reproducibility.`,
['Missing: delete, impute, flag – ask why', 'Outliers: error or genuine tail event?', 'Fix duplicates, units, formats, wrong labels']);
