  L('m2c1-6', 'm2c1', 'Data preparation techniques and their benefits',
`Beyond cleaning, preparation turns raw data into informative model inputs:

• **Feature engineering**: create ratios (debt/income), lags, rolling averages, interaction terms.
• **Feature selection**: drop irrelevant or redundant features to reduce noise, overfitting and cost.
• **Scaling/normalisation** so features are comparable (next objective).
• **Transformations** such as logs to reduce skew.
• **Dimensionality reduction** (PCA, autoencoders).
• **Handling imbalance**: oversampling (e.g. SMOTE), undersampling, class weights.
• **Splitting** into training, validation and test sets **before** fitting preprocessing steps to avoid **data leakage**.

