  L('m2c1-9', 'm2c1', 'Training, validation and test samples',
`• **Training set** (e.g. 60–70%): used to fit the model parameters.
• **Validation set** (e.g. 15–20%): used to compare models and **tune hyperparameters** (tree depth, regularisation strength) and for early stopping.
• **Test set** (e.g. 15–20%): kept untouched until the end to give an **unbiased estimate** of performance on new data. Use it once.

If you tune on the test set, the test score becomes optimistic. With little data, use **cross-validation** instead of a single validation split.

For time series, split **chronologically** (train on the past, test on the future) to avoid look-ahead bias.`,
['Train: fit parameters', 'Validation: tune hyperparameters / select model', 'Test: final unbiased estimate, use once', 'Time series: split in time order']);
