3. **Update** each centroid to the mean of the points assigned to it.
4. Repeat steps 2–3 until assignments stop changing (convergence).

The algorithm minimises the **within-cluster sum of squares (WCSS)**. It always converges, but possibly to a **local** minimum, so run it several times with different starts and keep the best (lowest WCSS).

Example: centroid A at (1, 1), centroid B at (5, 5). The point (2, 3) has squared distance 1+4 = 5 to A and 9+4 = 13 to B, so it joins A.`,
